Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: The Postmark Stings the Lacquer
- Story & Context: On the stalled 03:14 mail-commuter crawl through the Carlisle Freight Depot, Julian Vane wedged his battery-powered mini-synth between the unheated carriage window and a steel luggage rack, desperate to drown out the rhythmic clatter of flat-spotted wheelsets. The pungent stench of track creosote filled the freezing compartment as he struck a rusted cowbell with an allen key, only for a fellow insomniac clerk to angrily fling a bundle of delayed transit letters across the cabin. One unsealed envelope ignited against an exposed heating coil, showering the velvet-clad musicians with charred paper flakes while the pocket sequencer captured the sparks in a roaring loop of clipped distortion. Vane immediately belted the hook straight into an earphone mic: "Stamped red, stamped dead, running ten miles ahead."
