Track 2: Why Did You Send It Second Class?
- Story & Context: Huddled in the drafty vestibule of the Crewe night service where bleary-eyed third-shift workers shared headphone splitters to trade synthesized drum loops, Sorcha Vance wiped cold condensation from the frosted Plexiglas door. Her soot-dusted velvet cuffs reeked of copper grease as she fished out a rain-smeared envelope that had spent four weeks trapped beneath an iron sorting grate in the logistics terminal. Reading the belated telegram inside, she realized her lover had boarded an outbound cargo ferry a month prior, leaving her alone on the rails with a pocket drum machine hammering at 126 BPM. Trembling against the violent shudder of the carriage bogies, she hammered her cowbell with a brass luggage tag and cried out: "You spared two pennies to tell me you were gone."
